          "chapter": 4,
          "target_chapter": 4,
          "chapter_filter": "applied",
          "question": "Fair enough on the usability metrics, but I am troubled by the leap you've made regarding the system's performance. You suggest that the lower accuracy is merely a function of dataset scale, yet you also admit the app cannot handle multiple simultaneous conditions. Given that real-world rice samples frequently present with concurrent diseases, isn't it premature to focus on scale as the primary cause for the accuracy gap when the model's fundamental class-limitation seems to be the much larger obstacle to clinical validity?"
        }
